[size=5][b]Master Looter[/b][/size]
[i]Auto-loot for Crimson Desert 2.01.00 with an in-game menu.[/i]

Walk past it and it is in your bag: dropped items, herbs and flowers, ore and stone chunks, timber, insects, fish, small animals and animal carcasses. Each kind has its own switch. Every item is checked against a database of 6,813 items with classes and tags, and the game's own Take-or-Steal check decides what is off limits. Everything is set from a menu inside the game; there is no ini to edit.

[size=4][b]What it collects[/b][/size]
Twelve switches under Looting, each on its own:
[list]
[*]Ground items, including what enemies drop.
[*]Animal carcasses, skinned once each. Human corpses drop ordinary loot instead.
[*]Plants: herb, flower and mushroom nodes, and the same lying loose. Crops such as barley or sweet potatoes count as ground items whether on the plant or on the ground.
[*]Ore, stone and wood, as chunks on the ground and as nodes that yield them. Ore veins are still broken with your pickaxe; the chunks are picked up for you.
[*]Insects: butterflies, beetles, dragonflies, bees, spiders, scorpions, snails and the rest of what the game files as insects.
[*]Fish, and whatever else you catch in the water: crabs, shrimp, squid, starfish, seahorses.
[*]Small animals: rats, squirrels, birds, lizards, frogs, salamanders.
[*]Unidentified nodes, containers and furniture nodes, all off by default.
[/list]
Gather nodes are armed from a distance, so a bush fills its data without you standing on it. Each kind has its own range, and the scan pace is yours to set.

[size=4][b]What it leaves alone[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Anything the game would call stealing. The mod asks the same routine the game uses to decide between "Take" and "Steal", and walks past whatever would put a bounty on you. You can opt in under Looting, Ownership.
[*]Quest items, memory chips, puzzle and mechanism parts, artifacts, recipes and your own equipment. The Classes and Items tabs can lift most of that on purpose, per class or per item.
[*]Fast-travel artifacts, memory triggers, locked nodes, gear worn by others and the contents of storage stacks, always.
[/list]

[size=4][b]The menu[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]General: the auto-loot switch, a burst button, keys, scan pace and the filters (quest items, unsellable items, a copper value floor, unnamed items).
[*]Looting: the twelve switches, ranges, node arming and the ownership opt-in.
[*]Classes: one-click groups such as Weapons and armor, Damaged gear, Food and drink, Materials, Books and papers or Treasure and keepsakes, above a table of every class with its item count.
[*]Tags: always or never per tag; never beats always, and both beat the class rule.
[*]Items: search any of the 6,813 items, set an override, and see the verdict the rules give it right now.
[*]Presets: every setting and every rule saved under a name and swapped in two clicks. Settings are backed up each time the game starts and the last twelve are kept, so an update with different defaults is one button to undo. Anything that overwrites or discards asks first.
[*]A notice when the bag stops taking things. The game does not announce a full bag, so the mod watches what happens after a pick-up and tells you when nothing is arriving.
[*]Nearby: every object around you with its distance, class and the rule that decided it.
[*]Status: every signature and hook, the event path, counters, recent loot and the log.
[/list]
Watch mode keeps the menu on screen while you play, so you can read the Nearby list or the log with the controls still yours.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]With Definitive Mod Manager (DMM)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download the DMM file and import it (drag it onto the DMM window). DMM registers MasterLooter.asi as an ASI add-on.
[*]Remove or disable any other auto-loot mod. Two of them hook the same game functions and the second one to load does nothing.
[*]Enable it and Mount.
[/list]
[b]By hand[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Ultimate ASI Loader (winmm.dll) must be in the game's bin64 folder.
[*]Copy MasterLooter.asi into bin64 next to winmm.dll while the game is closed. The item database and the creature table are built into the plugin.
[*]Start the game and press Insert.
[/list]
Uninstall by deleting the MasterLooter.* files from bin64 (the plugin writes MasterLooter.ini and .log next to itself). No game file is modified and nothing is written to a save.

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Insert opens and closes the menu. Escape also closes it.
[*]F10 turns auto-loot on and off. F11 loots everything in range once.
[*]Home is watch mode: the menu stays up while the game keeps every input. Insert makes it interactive again.
[*]While the menu is interactive the game does not see keyboard, mouse or controller; key releases still pass so nothing sticks.
[/list]
All keys are rebindable under General. Hotkeys are ignored while the game window is not in front.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Built for Crimson Desert 2.01.00 (exe 1.0.0.2760). Every game address comes from a byte pattern or a class name resolved at load, so a small update does not necessarily break it; the Status tab shows what resolved and what did not, and the log says the same in more detail.
[*]Works with DLSS frame generation and HDR. The menu is drawn before frame generation and composited for the swap chain's colour space.
[*]Keyboard, mouse and controller are all handled while the menu is up.
[*]Requires Ultimate ASI Loader (winmm.dll) in bin64. DMM installs it for you.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Safety and known limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The mod sends the game the same events it sends itself when you press the interaction key, and reads memory only to decide what to send.
[*]A carcass is searched once per session and never again, whatever the retry setting: searching an empty carcass has been seen to duplicate items, and duplicates are how saves get corrupted.
[*]No line-of-sight check. Ranges are distances, not visibility. Keep the arming range short or a node behind a thin wall can be gathered.
[*]Creatures the mod cannot name are only caught when every category they could belong to is on. Bugs are recognised by their model, fish by theirs; a few unusual creatures may stay unidentified and be left alone.
[*]Gather nodes are identified by the prefab they were placed from, matched against a table of 1,042 node kinds built from the game's own data. A node outside that table is identified by what lands in your bag when it is gathered, and is otherwise left alone until you turn Unidentified nodes on.
[*]Chests and storage boxes open a window rather than hand over an item; they are off by default.
[*]Single player. Do not use it anywhere it would give you an advantage over other people.
[/list]

[size=4][b]If something is wrong[/b][/size]
MasterLooter.log next to the plugin is rewritten every launch. It lists which signatures resolved, and for every object within range that was skipped, once, the rule that skipped it. Post the relevant lines with a report: what was taken or left, where you were, and what you expected. A report is useful in both directions: something taken that should have stayed, or something left that should have been taken.

